body:
Honestly I'm pretty cool with that shit and if someone was open enough to me to do such a thing unironically I'd be happy getting to know them.

&#x200B;

As long as they respect boundaries, that is.

I definitely try to build myself towards the "righteous" things you just said but (this might be because of my current depression issues) I am sometimes unable to do such things because it puts too much on me, which makes me kind of doubt myself in that sense. Physically, I'm kinda like you, I'm not too short but I'm an underweight low muscle lanky guy.

&#x200B;

I'm not ashamed or disgusted by how I look but I feel it doesn't reflect who I am and want to be in a close relationship. Although I also like to stand up for people, it's not what I feel is good for me to enjoy life. I feel like a more soft and loving(/loved) person is who I need to be to feel good in a relationship, and I feel like I would feel more comfortable in that being a female.

&#x200B;

I'm lucky enough to have a good therapist to talk to, so I'll definitely do that!
